        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/general-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Bought from Morris & Co. as a kit, this panel was a very ambitious project. The finely worked result shows the high standard of amateur needlework among middle-class women at the  time. Mrs Battye was a good client of Morris & Co..  A panel incorporating the arms of the Battye family, drawn in the Morris Workshops and worked by her, is now in the William Morris Gallery, Walthamstow."@en ;
